      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T16:39:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Marco: I found that it is necessary to check if `cpi-\u003eunscaled_source` is null because `init_motion_estimation()` is also called before `av1_encode()` sets `cpi-\u003eunscaled_source` to `frame_input-\u003esource`.\n\nThis raises an interesting issue: `init_motion_estimation()` may be called when `cpi-\u003eunscaled_source` is uninitialized (null) or contains a stale value from the previous `aom_codec_encode()` call. Is this okay?\n\nIt seems that as long as `init_motion_estimation()` is eventually called with the correct value of `cpi-\u003eunscaled_source` before we perform motion search, the earlier calls with uninitialized or stale values of `cpi-\u003eunscaled_source` are wasteful but harmless.",
      "revId": "7a34bf6503f21162a5c651c46887ffe9421d05b1",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
